# Build-context filter for deploy/compose/Dockerfile.sealed.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's, so this
# is scoped to the VENDOR image and imposes nothing on the platform build beside it.
#
# The allow-list is three files, and the shortness is the point: a sealed vendor image
# that can see the platform's source tree during its build is one `COPY` away from
# carrying it. Compare `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, which admits the whole `medos` package
# because the platform image installs it.
*
!medos/medos/sealed/reference.py
!medos/deploy/sealed-reference/service.manifest.json
!medos/deploy/sealed-reference/weights.bin

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
